rsz: profile where a setup repair spends its wall time

Study instrumentation for the repair_timing runtime study; not for
upstream, and retired with the study branch.

With -verbose rsz prints one progress row per optimisation pass, so a
log already says how many passes a repair took and what each bought.
It does not say where the seconds inside a pass go: ranking the path's
targets, generating and estimating candidates, applying a move through
the ECO journal, re-estimating parasitics, the incremental required-time
update and the worst-slack scan after every pass, restoring a journal
when an endpoint did not improve, or the progress row itself, which
walks every vertex in the graph to collect violating startpoints.

This accumulates wall seconds into a RepairProfile on the run's shared
RepairSetupContext, using utl::DebugScopedTimer's aggregate form the way
Rebuffer.cc already does, and prints one key=value line per phase:

    [RSZ-PROFILE] phase=LEGACY* passes=1206 collect_s=... repair_path_s=...
        generate_s=... commit_s=... parasitics_s=... sta_s=... journal_s=...
        progress_s=... tns_s=... candidates=... attempts=... accepted=...

repair_path_s encloses generate_s and commit_s, sta_s encloses
worst_s (the worst-slack refresh after findRequireds), and journal_s
encloses restore_s; path_s is the worst-slack path lookup before each
pass, begin_s the per-endpoint setup, and phase_s the whole of each
profiled phase, so what the slices miss is a number too; the rest are
disjoint.
The line is emitted with logger->report so it needs no message id.
Nothing about the result changes: a binary with this patch produces the
same ODB as one without.

diff --git a/src/rsz/src/RepairSetupContext.hh b/src/rsz/src/RepairSetupContext.hh
index b85658abdc..c33004b5f2 100644
--- a/src/rsz/src/RepairSetupContext.hh
+++ b/src/rsz/src/RepairSetupContext.hh
@@ -9,6 +9,31 @@ namespace rsz {
 
 class Resizer;
 
+// Where a setup repair run spends its wall time, accumulated across
+// phases and printed once per phase. Study instrumentation: not for
+// upstream. Seconds unless named otherwise.
+struct RepairProfile
+{
+  double collect_s{0.0};      // collectViolatingEndpoints
+  double repair_path_s{0.0};  // repairPath, all of it
+  double generate_s{0.0};     // generator.generate + estimate, inside it
+  double commit_s{0.0};       // committer.commit (apply), inside it
+  double parasitics_s{0.0};   // updateParasitics after a pass
+  double sta_s{0.0};          // findRequireds + refreshEndpointSlacks
+  double worst_s{0.0};        // refreshEndpointSlacks alone, inside sta_s
+  double journal_s{0.0};      // begin/commit/restore journal
+  double restore_s{0.0};      // restoreJournal alone, inside journal_s
+  double path_s{0.0};         // vertexWorstSlackPath before each pass
+  double begin_s{0.0};        // beginEndpointRepair (journal begin, path, slacks)
+  double phase_s{0.0};        // whole iterate() of the profiled phases
+  double progress_s{0.0};     // printProgress (-verbose rows)
+  double tns_s{0.0};          // totalNegativeSlack in terminateProgress
+  long candidates{0};         // candidates generated
+  long attempts{0};           // commits attempted
+  long accepted{0};           // commits accepted
+  long passes{0};             // repairEndpoint passes (opto iterations)
+};
+
 struct RepairSetupContext
 {
   explicit RepairSetupContext(Resizer& resizer);
@@ -32,6 +57,7 @@ struct RepairSetupContext
   float initial_tns{0.0f};
   float previous_tns{0.0f};
   bool progress_header_printed{false};
+  RepairProfile profile;
 
   // Legacy-derived setup phases share one preamble per repair_setup run.
   bool legacy_preamble_done{false};
